Gherkin wrote:
> I have played nethack for years and just downloaded SLASH'EM for the
> first time.  However, the interface seems quite different, and I would
> prefer to play with ASCII characters.  Is it possible to play SLASHEM
> in ASCII graphics and with the same commands as regular nethack?  Maybe
> this is a stupid question, but I know very little about Nethack beyond
> how to enter my name and play.

Yes you can. That's how I play slashem (although you will find that the
interface is still a tiny bit different.)

The advice that follows is based on my own experience with the standard
windows executable for slashem. If you're on a different OS, my advice
may be less than useful:

Your defaults.nh file needs to look something like this:

[snip]
# *** Tilesets provided for use by plug-in window interfaces.
TILESET=name:Small tiles,file:gltile16.png
TILESET=name:Big tiles,file:gltile32.png,transparent
TILESET=name:Big 3D tiles,file:gltile64.png,transparent,pseudo3D
OPTIONS=tiles:Big tiles

# *** OPTIONS ***
#
# Use the TTY (console) window interface instead of the default GUI
interface.
# Note: This has no effect if you are using a plug-in window interface,
such
# as gtkhack.
OPTIONS=windowtype:tty

# Use the IBM character set rather than just plain ascii characters
# for tty window-port.
OPTIONS=IBMGraphics
[snip]

You may also need to copy one of the keyboard dll files over from your
vanilla nethack installation: I think it's nhdefkey.dll - compare the
two zips to see what (if anything) is missing.



